WEBVTT

00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:03.690
<b>It has begun</b>

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:03.470
It has begun.

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:07.360
We angels—

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:17.240
we wingless, fallen angels—
 are about to be killed off, one by one,

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.980
by the true angels in heaven.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:23.570
How foolish.

00:00:23.570 --> 00:00:28.430
If the executor were an angel, 
they would have no trouble killing us.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:30.260
They'd need only play their trumpets.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:33.720
They would have no reason
 to resort to physical means.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.950
This is a serial murder meant 
to look like an angel's bidding,

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.720
carried out by someone here.

00:00:40.430 --> 00:00:44.900
"The angels shall bring true 
death upon the performers. V."

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:47.060
V?

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:48.940
Is that not foolish in itself?

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:53.750
We have no reason to kill one another.

00:00:53.750 --> 00:00:57.550
What good would it do us to kill our own kind?

00:00:58.340 --> 00:00:59.910
What do you think, Leader?

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:01.310
Leader!

00:01:01.800 --> 00:01:02.660
Leader!

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.440
Leader!

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:14.840
Is this the punishment given to us 
fallen angels for adoring humanity?

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:19.690
Angels have been sent from 
the heavens to purge us.

00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:24.590
They are called "Gifted."

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:26.610
"Gifted"?

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:28.350
"Gifted"?

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.370
Hey. What's a Gifted?

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:33.270
We are humans. We are of the earth,

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:31.930
Just watch, and it'll make sense.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:36.700
having rejected being angels 
and choosing to become human.

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:37.520
<i>Who is he?</i>

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:43.910
We dream, we love, and seek fulfillment 
possible only because we are finite.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:40.250
Hey, can I ask something?

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:45.110
The people here are paying 
to watch this, right?

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:46.770
And we do not regret that decision.

00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:48.100
Why doesn't anyone get upset at
 being forced to sit through a show

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:51.780
To choose one's own way of being
 is the truest form of the soul.

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:49.200
with such an obvious ending?

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:50.180
Hey.

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:53.470
He's the murderer, isn't he?

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:52.420
Indeed.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:54.920
And angels and humans are of 
entirely different dimensions.

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:55.750
You can tell in the first five minutes.

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.700
Angels cannot have the fulfillment 
which is the realm of humanity,

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:58.120
Knock it off!

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:00.630
and humans are incapable of 
the supremacy of angels.

00:01:59.190 --> 00:02:00.270
Why?

00:02:00.630 --> 00:02:04.080
Those who control humans from the 
outside and those who enjoy fulfillment

00:02:00.860 --> 00:02:04.870
Why is everyone watching this 
play without complaining?

00:02:04.080 --> 00:02:07.330
on the inside are like an author and their
 characters: never shall they intertwine.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:06.470
It really upsets me.

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:09.100
I don't get it.

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:08.240
And yet...

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:09.090
And yet?

00:02:09.090 --> 00:02:10.230
And yet?

00:02:10.230 --> 00:02:14.110
There are those who, despite being human, have 
some fragment of angels' forbidden supremacy.

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:15.310
There's something everyone 
else gets that I don't.

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:17.270
That is, oh, that is truly the cursed 
soul that we call Gifted.

00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:17.320
I don't get it.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.360
None of us can possibly be 
as sinful as the Gifted.

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:18.030
I'm scared.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:22.060
It's like the world is filled with monsters,

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.470
The accursed Gifted snuff us out 
one by one like prey for the hunt.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:24.490
monsters that only I don't understand.

00:02:22.470 --> 00:02:24.490
We must find these Gifted.

00:02:24.490 --> 00:02:26.370
No, perhaps we must first hire a detective?

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:28.270
I'm all alone,

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.890
living in a world of monsters.

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:36.730
<i>There will now be a fifteen 
minute intermission.</i>

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:40.420
<i>The second act will resume at 6:20.</i>

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:42.920
Come.

00:02:45.520 --> 00:02:48.420
I'll give you the answer you're looking for.

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:55.030
Have your parents said 
anything about your talents?

00:02:55.030 --> 00:02:56.340
Talents?

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:58.420
I wish I had talent.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:00.210
It wouldn't be so hard to find work.

00:03:00.410 --> 00:03:01.250
No.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:04.190
You have a special talent.

00:03:05.090 --> 00:03:06.680
You were right.

00:03:07.280 --> 00:03:09.780
I used to carry a sword on my waist.

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:15.080
I was known as the Master of Swords, 
even within the government's ranks.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:20.070
My sword would bring peace to the nation.

00:03:20.070 --> 00:03:21.780
...or so I sincerely believed.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:23.980
That's why I killed.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.260
Assassination was far too easy.

00:03:27.550 --> 00:03:30.000
I only became fearful when I noticed

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.310
that I was waiting eagerly 
for the next assassination.

00:03:33.920 --> 00:03:40.370
I could no longer tell whether I was murdering 
for my country or for the moment of the kill.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:45.410
That's when I decided
 I'd never wield a sword again.

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:51.330
No one else has ever learned 
of my past occupation.

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:55.450
You guessed the murderer 
in the play earlier.

00:03:56.110 --> 00:04:00.720
I suspect you are the only one who 
could have gleaned the answer so quickly.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:03.710
I wouldn't have known if I hadn't 
read the script, either.

00:04:04.740 --> 00:04:08.340
Have you ever thought that the 
people around you are all fools?

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:12.150
That they're all clueless idiots?

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:17.080
Yes.

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:19.590
Listen, and remember this.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:21.410
You are special.

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:23.410
Other people <i>are</i> all fools.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:25.410
Including me.

00:04:26.010 --> 00:04:30.730
The reason you're alone is because 
you have a special talent.

00:04:30.730 --> 00:04:31.980
Special?

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:35.460
But abilities need to be controlled.

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:39.820
For you to pretend not 
to notice your own talent

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:45.060
is the same as my past self, 
swinging a sword in pursuit of blood.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:47.170
I'm the only one who's special?

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:49.410
How could that even happen?

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:52.690
Look at all the people in this city.

00:04:55.410 --> 00:04:56.540
Well...

00:04:56.540 --> 00:04:57.950
Well?

00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:01.320
Because you're Gifted.

00:05:03.220 --> 00:05:06.490
You're special because you're Gifted.

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:08.910
Gifted?

00:05:08.910 --> 00:05:13.430
Your ability is one that allows you to 
determine the truth at a single glance.

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:19.430
There are numerous people 
with special gifts in this world.

00:05:20.110 --> 00:05:26.060
It's because of your special ability that 
the people around you look like monsters.

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:29.480
You must control your ability.

00:05:30.130 --> 00:05:32.040
I'll teach you how.

00:05:32.670 --> 00:05:35.190
With the help of a certain individual,

00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:38.560
you'll become able to produce 
your special ability on command.

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:39.970
A certain individual?

00:05:41.070 --> 00:05:42.000
Here.

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:44.450
Glasses?

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:50.420
These were handed down
 by a noble man from Kyoto.

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:54.460
When you wear them, 
your ability will be activated,

00:05:54.460 --> 00:05:57.750
and the truth will come to you instantly.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:05:59.980
And, when you aren't wearing them,

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:02.700
you will no longer be bothered 
by the foolishness of others.

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:04.990
I'll give them to you.

00:06:07.750 --> 00:06:10.800
These just look like a really 
cheap pair of glasses.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.170
<i>Correct.</i>

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:15.320
<i>They're a leftover I was forced 
to buy at a trinket shop.</i>

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:17.150
<i>But...</i>

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:18.780
I don't see a difference.

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:26.120
Now, use those glasses to 
control your special ability.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:31.060
Control my special ability?

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:32.600
That's right.

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:35.200
Cut open the truth with your special ability

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:39.040
and banish evil from the darkness
 in which it lurks, Gifted detective!

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:43.000
From today on, you are the 
world's best detective.

00:06:43.260 --> 00:06:44.890
Best detective?

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:47.440
Isn't everything clear to you now?

00:06:48.290 --> 00:06:51.030
The world isn't terrifying at all.

00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:53.270
No one is a monster.

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:56.400
They're simply far more 
foolish than you are.

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:57.970
Really?

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:01.400
No one bears any ill will towards you.

00:07:01.400 --> 00:07:03.340
They're stupid idiots.

00:07:03.340 --> 00:07:06.000
Mere children who don't 
know how to see the world.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.360
Children?

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:09.820
Everyone's just a stupid idiot?

00:07:09.820 --> 00:07:10.820
Yes.

00:07:11.080 --> 00:07:14.240
They actually don't know anything?

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:15.450
That's right.

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:17.210
But...

00:07:17.210 --> 00:07:18.870
Edogawa Rampo!

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:22.590
The glasses have already accepted you.

00:07:22.590 --> 00:07:25.090
All that's left is for 
you to open your mind.

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:27.490
Open my mind?

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:32.180
This creepy world...

00:07:32.580 --> 00:07:36.880
That time, that time, that time, 
and that time...

00:07:37.900 --> 00:07:42.390
All that suffering wasn't because 
there's something wrong with me,

00:07:42.390 --> 00:07:45.520
but because there's something 
wrong with the people around me?

00:07:48.790 --> 00:07:50.660
Is that what it means?

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:53.750
They are all clueless children.

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:58.240
Would a baby who can't even hold 
its head up ever despise another?

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:00.640
<i>He's right...</i>

00:08:07.440 --> 00:08:10.800
No one ever despised me.

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:24.330
I see!

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:25.720
You're all babies!

00:08:25.720 --> 00:08:28.450
The world isn't creepy at all!

00:08:28.450 --> 00:08:31.400
You're just all stupid little idiots!

00:08:31.680 --> 00:08:34.800
I have to protect all these silly children!

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:36.590
Come on, Rampo...

00:08:36.590 --> 00:08:38.240
There's something I have to do.

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:40.850
You head back to your seat, mister.

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:43.930
We still might be able to stop the murder.

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:45.150
What?

00:08:45.150 --> 00:08:49.440
The murderer will follow through with 
their threat and commit the attack.

00:08:49.950 --> 00:08:52.100
We just have to take advantage of that fact.

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:53.910
What are you talking about?

00:08:53.910 --> 00:08:56.290
I already see everything.

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:59.290
The enemy's goals,
 their plans, everything.

00:08:59.690 --> 00:09:03.840
So I want you to keep 
an eye on the audience.

00:09:05.960 --> 00:09:06.860
All right.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:09.050
But be careful.

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:10.660
Don't worry!

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:17.030
After all, I'm the world's best detective, 
on a mission to protect the world's fools!

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:50.040
Episode 39

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:50.040
<b><i>The Day Is a Dream, The Night Is Real</i></b>

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:50.040
<b><i>m 0 0 l 450 0 450 80 0 80
</i></b>

00:10:51.400 --> 00:10:54.500
Forgive us, haloed angel of war,

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:57.700
or show yourself in the human realm!

00:10:58.110 --> 00:11:00.340
I do not fear death!

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:05.050
If you must cast judgment, 
first pierce my chest.

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:07.020
I know what you want.

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:10.080
You want me to watch as my 
friends spite one another

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:12.610
with the foulness common 
to humanity, don't you?

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:14.350
I shall expose you!

00:11:14.350 --> 00:11:16.030
And your sin!

00:11:29.630 --> 00:11:31.090
Wow.

00:11:31.650 --> 00:11:34.210
<i>This doesn't happen in the script.</i>

00:11:36.190 --> 00:11:37.090
Why's he...?

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:41.060
<i>Real blood.</i>

00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:41.970
Call an ambulance!

00:11:42.280 --> 00:11:45.530
Inform the police at the 
door and close the theater.

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:48.270
<i>Is he dead?</i>

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:50.430
<i>But where's the weapon?</i>

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:53.050
<i>No weapon...</i>

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:54.660
No...

00:11:54.940 --> 00:11:56.430
A murder by an angel?

00:11:57.410 --> 00:11:58.450
Impossible!

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:01.610
No!

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:04.870
Takio!

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:06.440
He's actually dead!

00:12:05.890 --> 00:12:07.690
It's a murder!

00:12:08.580 --> 00:12:10.060
Stay in your seats!

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:14.210
If you flee, you could become 
a suspect in the murder.

00:12:10.840 --> 00:12:14.830
Takio! Takio!

00:12:18.790 --> 00:12:22.590
So I want you to keep 
an eye on the audience.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:25.110
<i>So the one who flees is the culprit.</i>

00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:35.650
<i>Where has Rampo gone?</i>

00:12:36.230 --> 00:12:39.200
Captain, a member of the 
audience has disappeared.

00:12:39.200 --> 00:12:40.280
What?

00:12:40.840 --> 00:12:42.020
Pardon me.

00:12:43.600 --> 00:12:46.010
Why, hello, sir.

00:12:46.010 --> 00:12:47.310
Thank you for your work.

00:12:47.310 --> 00:12:49.690
I overheard that someone 
fled from the audience.

00:12:49.690 --> 00:12:50.420
Yes.

00:12:50.810 --> 00:12:54.610
I'm sure we handled the lockdown 
of the theater competently,

00:12:54.610 --> 00:12:55.870
but someone has vanished.

00:12:55.870 --> 00:12:58.570
What does this person look like 
and which seat were they in?

00:12:58.570 --> 00:13:00.490
He was in the front row.

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:02.700
Light-brown suit and a round hat.

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:07.430
A dignified-looking, middle-aged man, 
holding a wooden cane.

00:13:08.570 --> 00:13:09.860
<i>It's that man.</i>

00:13:10.270 --> 00:13:12.730
When did that man leave his seat?

00:13:12.730 --> 00:13:16.780
We have confirmation that he was there 
when the performance began, but...

00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:20.260
I'm going to search the building.

00:13:20.260 --> 00:13:22.150
Wait, sir!

00:13:22.430 --> 00:13:23.810
<i>This is my fault.</i>

00:13:23.810 --> 00:13:25.690
<i>I instigated this.</i>

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:29.030
<i>Rampo's just a boy. He doesn't 
know how to protect himself.</i>

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:33.450
<i>He may be a brilliant detective,</i>

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:37.940
<i>but if the murderer attacks him
 in a frenzy, he doesn't stand a chance.</i>

00:13:39.280 --> 00:13:41.800
<i>He can't activate his ability on his own.</i>

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:45.000
<i>I need to become his 
shield and fend off evil,</i>

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:48.550
<i>so he's safe to engage in his reasoning.</i>

00:13:52.220 --> 00:13:56.270
<b>A 
detective
 must
 be
 armed</b>

00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:55.970
<i>A detective must be armed.</i>

00:13:58.450 --> 00:13:59.810
Fukuzawa-san.

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:05.410
Sorry, but please make it quick.

00:14:05.940 --> 00:14:08.160
I have a message from Rampo-kun.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:09.110
Yes?

00:14:09.730 --> 00:14:13.880
Rampo-kun said there were two murderers.

00:14:14.400 --> 00:14:17.860
This crime is comprised of 
two different kinds of acts.

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:19.910
You could think of it like 
a shrimp and a sea bream.

00:14:20.550 --> 00:14:24.070
You could be satisfied with the shrimp,
 which is easy to catch.

00:14:24.070 --> 00:14:25.790
Shrimp's pretty tasty.

00:14:26.110 --> 00:14:28.930
But if you want to catch the sea bream,

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:32.640
well, you're going to 
have to use the shrimp.

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:34.740
<i>That's so convoluted.</i>

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:37.090
Where is Rampo?

00:14:37.090 --> 00:14:38.300
Dunno.

00:14:38.300 --> 00:14:40.600
He could be anywhere.

00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:44.810
Murakami was the one who was 
murdered, so why talk to me?

00:14:45.150 --> 00:14:48.830
Because Rampo-kun told me the
 truth about part of the case.

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:54.140
Fukuzawa-san, who is that kid?

00:14:54.140 --> 00:14:57.580
I have no doubt that he's 
an excellent detective,

00:14:57.580 --> 00:15:02.680
but is he really Gifted, 
the way he says he is?

00:15:03.390 --> 00:15:04.590
What happened?

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:07.640
He's the only one who 
sees the whole picture.

00:15:08.080 --> 00:15:12.950
"I'm going to solve the whole thing, 
so get your butt to the seats," he said.

00:15:23.740 --> 00:15:29.400
I am the deus ex machina, here to solve
 the case at the very end of this play!

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:33.990
Basically, I'm Gifted 
and a brilliant detective.

00:15:34.330 --> 00:15:37.660
Anyway, let's get to the chapter 
where it's all solved.

00:15:37.890 --> 00:15:41.930
I was listening to the murmuring earlier.

00:15:41.930 --> 00:15:46.620
It seems like a lot of you 
think the angel killed him.

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:50.910
Just so you know, angels...

00:15:51.670 --> 00:15:52.540
do exist.

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:56.220
You, the audience, are the angels.

00:15:56.880 --> 00:16:00.680
This murder and this play 
are deeply connected.

00:16:01.160 --> 00:16:03.620
This play is about a turning of tides.

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:05.690
The tables turn between 
the angels and humans,

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:08.510
and the executors become the executed.

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:10.850
There's an empty seat there.

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:16.460
The municipal police think the gentleman who 
vanished from that seat is the culprit.

00:16:16.970 --> 00:16:19.850
But this is a story about a reversal.

00:16:19.850 --> 00:16:21.690
The power dynamic shifts,

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:24.540
and the victim and attacker swap seats.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:26.890
In other words, he isn't the attacker.

00:16:28.210 --> 00:16:29.880
He's the victim.

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:34.170
And the victim was here all along.

00:16:38.290 --> 00:16:40.390
This is the turning of the tide.

00:16:47.060 --> 00:16:49.530
And thus the attacker has become the victim.

00:16:50.180 --> 00:16:53.040
Now, policemen, it's your turn.

00:16:54.120 --> 00:16:55.750
He's just unconscious.

00:16:55.750 --> 00:16:57.470
You don't have to be in such a hurry.

00:16:58.960 --> 00:17:02.740
Now, here's the elephant in the room.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:08.170
Who is that man and why did 
he have to be abducted?

00:17:08.170 --> 00:17:12.090
You could obviously ask the attacker.

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:16.650
There was never a murder to begin with.

00:17:17.170 --> 00:17:21.600
Now, show yourself, fallen one!

00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:28.010
What?!

00:17:31.140 --> 00:17:32.600
When did you realize?

00:17:32.970 --> 00:17:34.640
From the beginning.

00:17:34.640 --> 00:17:36.780
When I first met you in the green room,

00:17:36.780 --> 00:17:40.450
you looked pale and you were 
chugging a ton of water.

00:17:40.900 --> 00:17:43.190
That was because you'd just drawn blood.

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:47.530
In order to throw off the security police, 
the municipal police, and the forensic experts,

00:17:47.530 --> 00:17:50.450
you had to use your own fresh blood.

00:17:50.450 --> 00:17:54.790
To fake your own pulse, you used the 
silicon rubber stuff you use in plays.

00:17:56.720 --> 00:18:01.480
You needed the stagewright's 
cooperation to pull off this play.

00:18:01.890 --> 00:18:03.440
He's an accomplice, isn't he?

00:18:03.670 --> 00:18:04.930
That's right.

00:18:04.930 --> 00:18:07.540
The stagewright and I planned it together.

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:12.650
To think that an impossible Gifted 
would show up as a detective...

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:15.020
Not just any detective. The <i>best</i> detective.

00:18:15.400 --> 00:18:16.510
I am...

00:18:17.240 --> 00:18:19.740
I'm an actor.

00:18:20.190 --> 00:18:25.190
I become something I'm not and
 build a life that doesn't exist,

00:18:25.190 --> 00:18:29.380
all to carry out my job of 
exposing what humanity truly is.

00:18:29.790 --> 00:18:33.250
There's something unavoidable when 
you're trying to dramatize a way of life.

00:18:33.250 --> 00:18:34.880
That is death.

00:18:35.280 --> 00:18:39.920
My ultimate task was to play a real death.

00:18:40.370 --> 00:18:43.300
To me, that is what it means to 
reach the pinnacle of acting.

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:47.210
I am the first ever actor to play death.

00:18:47.210 --> 00:18:52.200
I wanted the audience here to see that.

00:18:54.160 --> 00:18:55.600
I have no regrets.

00:18:56.730 --> 00:18:58.810
This is how I live my life.

00:19:01.210 --> 00:19:02.830
I think you're amazing.

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:05.410
That's not something anyone can do.

00:19:05.770 --> 00:19:07.560
Speaking of which...

00:19:07.560 --> 00:19:10.800
Look at all the faces in the audience.

00:19:14.100 --> 00:19:17.550
Everyone here has two things in common.

00:19:18.200 --> 00:19:22.020
One is that they came 
specifically to see your play.

00:19:22.420 --> 00:19:27.220
The other is that they've witnessed 
a person's death up close.

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:33.020
I'm not really sure, but does forcing 
the audience make such a face...

00:19:34.560 --> 00:19:37.680
really count as the pinnacle of acting?

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:48.320
I see...

00:19:49.620 --> 00:19:54.210
I was doing all this acting for myself.

00:20:05.970 --> 00:20:07.170
Rampo.

00:20:07.170 --> 00:20:10.080
These glasses are awesome, mister!

00:20:10.080 --> 00:20:12.390
About that...

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:17.850
With these glasses and my special ability,
 I'm going to be unstoppable!

00:20:17.850 --> 00:20:20.320
Thank you, sirs!

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:24.280
Ever since I saw you, security policeman,

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:27.740
I was convinced that you 
would solve the case.

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:31.960
I never would have thought you'd 
have such a secret weapon.

00:20:31.960 --> 00:20:33.160
About that...

00:20:33.740 --> 00:20:39.500
I believe we must have you explain the 
resolution of the case at our station.

00:20:39.500 --> 00:20:42.130
Sure, but can I have that in my permit?

00:20:42.430 --> 00:20:46.350
"It's all thanks to my special 
abilities that we solved the case!"

00:20:46.350 --> 00:20:47.360
Just kidding.

00:20:48.150 --> 00:20:49.380
You're Gifted?!

00:20:49.380 --> 00:20:50.730
Like in the play?

00:20:51.080 --> 00:20:52.040
Amazing!

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:54.770
Our young detective is Gifted?!

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:55.900
That's right.

00:20:55.900 --> 00:20:58.330
A Gifted crime-solver.

00:20:58.330 --> 00:21:00.720
Brilliant detective Edogawa Rampo,
 at your service!

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:01.690
Hold it.

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:05.700
Sir, I'll handle the police hearing.

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:09.160
Rampo is exhausted from his detective work.

00:21:09.160 --> 00:21:11.620
Huh? I'm totally fine.

00:21:11.620 --> 00:21:16.010
You simply inferred the truth 
through observation and deduction.

00:21:16.010 --> 00:21:18.120
You never used any special ability.

00:21:18.780 --> 00:21:20.380
What are you talking about?

00:21:20.380 --> 00:21:23.020
You're the one who said I'm Gifted.

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:24.600
I'm telling you...

00:21:24.600 --> 00:21:27.190
Come on, do you seriously think

00:21:27.190 --> 00:21:30.010
I could have instantly seen through 
the case if I wasn't Gifted?

00:21:30.010 --> 00:21:31.260
I don't think so!

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:37.560
If the police are going to suck up to me, 
now's the time to do it!

00:21:38.260 --> 00:21:41.110
The ability to solve crimes instantly

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:44.600
is a godly power that 
can threaten the police's jobs.

00:21:44.600 --> 00:21:45.370
Sir!

00:21:45.710 --> 00:21:48.190
I can't wait to ride in the police car!

00:21:48.760 --> 00:21:53.640
Seems like this is going to take you a while,
 so I'll see you there, mister.

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:55.680
All right.

00:21:56.360 --> 00:21:58.990
I'm going to discuss the cleanup 
tasks with Egawa-san.

00:21:59.430 --> 00:22:00.730
I'll see you there.

00:22:01.640 --> 00:22:03.620
Officer, please take care of Rampo.

00:22:04.070 --> 00:22:05.340
Understood!

00:22:05.810 --> 00:22:06.580
Bye.

00:22:11.900 --> 00:22:13.210
Fukuzawa-san!

00:22:14.210 --> 00:22:16.680
See ya later!

00:22:23.090 --> 00:22:25.590
Fukuzawa-san, huh?

00:22:27.690 --> 00:22:29.090
Do you have a moment?

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:31.090
Fukuzawa-san.

00:22:31.090 --> 00:22:32.770
May I ask you something?

00:22:33.330 --> 00:22:36.630
Who was the man that was 
unconscious for a while?

00:22:37.760 --> 00:22:42.070
I'm told that the gentleman is 
the other aim of this project.

00:22:42.780 --> 00:22:43.920
You were <i>told?</i>

00:22:44.210 --> 00:22:48.680
I planned this project with 
the stagewright, Kurahashi.

00:22:48.680 --> 00:22:51.540
But he seemed to have plans of his own.

00:22:52.040 --> 00:22:55.820
The gentleman in the suit 
rarely appears in public.

00:22:55.820 --> 00:22:58.990
Apparently, capturing him 
was one of the objectives.

00:22:59.900 --> 00:23:01.620
Fukuzawa-sensei!

00:23:01.620 --> 00:23:04.320
Has the victim been here the whole time?

00:23:04.320 --> 00:23:05.100
What's the matter?

00:23:05.830 --> 00:23:08.330
The stagewright's been 
murdered in his room!

00:23:08.630 --> 00:23:09.450
What?!

00:23:09.450 --> 00:23:10.770
No...

00:23:11.210 --> 00:23:14.230
There doesn't seem to be any 
sign of a struggle at the scene.

00:23:14.670 --> 00:23:19.340
He's been impaled from 
behind in his own, locked room.

00:23:22.980 --> 00:23:24.930
A murder in a closed room?

00:23:25.360 --> 00:23:27.310
What is going on?

00:23:30.080 --> 00:23:32.610
Hey, officer, are we there yet?

00:23:33.590 --> 00:23:34.800
Soon.

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:40.010
Next Episode: 40

00:23:37.020 --> 00:23:40.010
<i>Secrets 
of the
 Founding
 of the 
Detective
 Agency</i>

00:23:37.510 --> 00:23:39.110
Mm-hm.
